# SPEC GOLDEN — hand-derived from css-flexbox-1 §9.6 step 1 (auto cross
# margins) and §9.4 (positions are inside the container's content box) before
# the code existed. Never regenerated.
#
# One row with `padding: 1em 2em` — 1 row above and below, 4 cells left and
# right — so its content box is x = 4, y = 1, w = 32. Every item is placed
# from *that* corner, not from the border box: a container's padding is space
# no item may be in, on either axis.
#
# Four 6-cell items (`flex: 0 0 48px`) of 6-cell words, at x = 4, 10, 16, 22.
# Item c is 5 rows of content, so the line's cross size is 5 and the row's
# border box is 1 + 5 + 1 = 7 rows.
#
# The container asks for `align-items: center`. Then:
#
#   a  `align-self: flex-start` overrides the container — and `margin-top` and
#      `margin-bottom: auto` override *that*, because §9.6 hands the free space
#      to auto margins before the alignment property is ever read. 4 free rows
#      split two and two, so the item is centred after all, by a different rule
#      than the container's and with its margin box filling the line:
#      y = 1 + 2 = 3.
#
#   b  one auto margin takes all 4 rows, which is how an item pins itself to
#      the cross-end edge of a row: y = 1 + 4 = 5.
#
#   c  fills the line, so `center` has nothing to give it: y = 1.
#
#   d  3 rows in a 5-row line, centred: y = 1 + 1 = 2.
#
# Nothing here is stretched: `align-items: center` is not `stretch`, so every
# item keeps the height its own content gave it.
<html>  x=0 y=0 w=40 h=7
  <body>  x=0 y=0 w=40 h=7
    <div.row> flex row  x=4 y=1 w=32 h=5
      <div.both>  x=4 y=3 w=6 h=1
        anonymous  x=4 y=3 w=6 h=1
          line  x=4 y=3 w=6 h=1
            #text "aaaaaa"  x=4 y=3 w=6 h=1
      <div.push>  x=10 y=5 w=6 h=1
        anonymous  x=10 y=5 w=6 h=1
          line  x=10 y=5 w=6 h=1
            #text "bbbbbb"  x=10 y=5 w=6 h=1
      <div>  x=16 y=1 w=6 h=5
        anonymous  x=16 y=1 w=6 h=5
          line  x=16 y=1 w=6 h=1
            #text "cccccc"  x=16 y=1 w=6 h=1
          line  x=16 y=2 w=6 h=1
            #text "dddddd"  x=16 y=2 w=6 h=1
          line  x=16 y=3 w=6 h=1
            #text "eeeeee"  x=16 y=3 w=6 h=1
          line  x=16 y=4 w=6 h=1
            #text "ffffff"  x=16 y=4 w=6 h=1
          line  x=16 y=5 w=6 h=1
            #text "gggggg"  x=16 y=5 w=6 h=1
      <div>  x=22 y=2 w=6 h=3
        anonymous  x=22 y=2 w=6 h=3
          line  x=22 y=2 w=6 h=1
            #text "hhhhhh"  x=22 y=2 w=6 h=1
          line  x=22 y=3 w=6 h=1
            #text "iiiiii"  x=22 y=3 w=6 h=1
          line  x=22 y=4 w=6 h=1
            #text "jjjjjj"  x=22 y=4 w=6 h=1
